hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16770","Abd Allah said: Abu Mamar narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sayyar informed us, from Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Qasri, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his grandfather Yazid ibn Asad: Love for people what you love for yourself."
"16771","Abd Allah said: Uqba ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutayba narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Ismail ibn Awsat, from Khalid ibn Abd Allah, from his grandfather Asad ibn Kurz, he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The sick man, his sins fall as the leaves of the tree fall."
"16772","Abd Allah said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ruzzi Abu Jafar narrated to me, he said: Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymuna narrated to us, he said: Sayyar narrated to us that he heard Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Qasri preaching on the minbar saying: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you love Paradise; he said: I said: Yes; he said: Then love for your brother what you love for yourself."
"16773","Abd Allah said: Abu al-Hasan Uthman ibn Abi Shayba at Kufa in the year two hundred thirty, and Yaqub al-Dawraqi, narrated to me, they said: Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba said: Sayyar informed us, he said: I heard Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Qasri on the minbar say: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather Yazid ibn Asad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Yazid ibn Asad, love for people what you love for yourself."
